    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "considerations-best-practices"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Considerations & Best Practices"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "blockquote",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "p",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Important:"
         ]
        },
        " Always test this pattern thoroughly in a sandbox tenant before promoting it to your production environment to ensure it behaves exactly as expected."
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Permissions & Credential Handling:"
         ]
        },
        " Ensure your service account or Personal Access Token (PAT) used to execute these external workflows follows the principle of least privilege, granting only the necessary authorization scopes (e.g., ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "idn:campaigns:manage"
         ]
        },
        "). Avoid hardcoding credentials in plain text."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "External Trigger Security:"
         ]
        },
        " When exposing workflows via external triggers, securely manage the generated Client ID and Secret. Treat them as sensitive credentials, rotate them periodically, and restrict their usage to authorized internal callers."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Safe Retry Behavior for POST Requests:"
         ]
        },
        " Be cautious when retrying HTTP POST operations. Ensure the target endpoint is idempotent or that you are properly handling potential duplicate resource creations if a request times out but was actually processed by the destination server."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
